=== layout: subsection

# Make the Group Work

=== layout: two-panels

# Before You Leave the Breakout Room

@left

## Agree on the People

- Confirm your group of 3-4 students.
- Exchange a communication method everyone will actually check.
- Put the next meeting on your calendars.
- Start one shared document for ideas, evidence, and decisions.

@right

## Agree on the Direction

- Shortlist the company ideas you want to develop.
- Name the specific product and the biological mechanism.
- Ask what new depth the group can add to the original pitch.
- Decide who will bring which evidence to your next meeting.

@notes

Visit the breakout rooms. Help students find a group and narrow an idea. These prompts organize the work; they are not an additional graded submission.

=== layout: two-panels

# Pick One Product You Can Explain

@left

## Too Broad

- A company that cures cancer.
- Better crops for everyone.
- A platform that does all the things.

@right

## A Direction You Can Research

- Which cancer, target, engineered cell, and measurable response?
- Which crop, trait, biological change, and comparison?
- Which first product, customer, competitor, and development milestone?

=== layout: one-panel

# One Company, One Shared Vision

@body

- Your group can change the name, market, product, or scientific strategy.
- Keep the useful feedback from the individual proposals.
- Explain what the new team brings to the science.
- Select the product by completing the [*Company Vision Report (Form), due Nov 19.*]{color=red}
- Submit the form once per group using the link on Blackboard.
